HTMl - Hyper text markup language

- To create a Web pages
- its not a programming language
- its a markup language
- Every website can start with HTML

1. Heading - h1 to h6

2. Paragraph - p

3. hr

4. br

5. Text formating - u, i, b or strong, mark, sup and sub

6. Anchor Tag - a

7. Image Tag - img

8. list - order list and unorder list

9. Tables - tr, th and td

10. Forms - input and label

11. Media Elements - Audio and video

12. Sematic Tags - Header, footer, main, section and nav

CSS - Cadcasing Style Sheet

1. Types of CSS
   i - Inline
   ii - internal
   iii - External
   inline > internal > external

2. CSS Synatax
   Selector{
   property: value;
   }

3. Types of Selector

4. Element Selector - (h1) (h2) (p)
5. Class Selector - (.) - Multiple times we can use the same class name, number of times
6. Id Selector - (#) - Unique - Only one time we can use the same id name
7. Universal Selector - (\*) - To apply the style in entire site
8. Group Selector - calss name or id name containes different tags we want to the same style maans we go for the group selector

9. Colors and Background  
   color: red;
   background-color: green;
   background-image: url(./Assets/Spider-Man.jpg);
   background-repeat: no-repeat;
   background-size: cover;
   background-position: center;

10. Text Styling
    font-family: Verdana, Geneva, Tahoma, sans-serif;
    font-size: 30px;
    text-align: start;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    text-decoration: underline;
    font-weight: bold;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: 20px;

11. Box Modeling
    margin
    border
    padding
    content

12. Flex(Display)
  1. Flex direction - row, row-reverse, column, column-reverse
  2. Justify content - (X) - start, center, end, space-around, space-evenly, space-between
  3. Align-items - (Y) - start, center, end
  4. Flex-wrap - nowrap, wrap, wrap-reverse
  5. Align-content - (Y) - (if only Flex wrap is enable then only it will act) - start, center, end, space-around, space-evenly, space-between
  6. Flex(items) - using flex:1 it will the enpty space
  7. gap - to be assign values like px,em,%,cm,m
  8. order - Change the visual order of the flex items

13. Position 
  1. Static (default)
  2. Relative - 
  3. Abdolute
  4. Fixed
  5. Sticky 

14. Grid (Display) - 2 dimensional layout system

15. Tranition and Animation
   Tranition - Whenever you just hover that the action will act
   Animation - Simply refresh the site the Animation will act

16. Media Queries or Responsive Design
   mobile - 320px to 600px
   tablet - 601px to 800px
   lap/desktop - above 801px  